#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:1
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding decorative elements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid "Apply Texture"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Apply Texture</emphasis> is a tool for applying "
"decorative textures to an image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:17 editor-decorate.docbook:74
#: editor-decorate.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By adding texture to your image, whether color or black and white, you can "
"make it look like an oil painting on canvas, an Old Masters etching, a Pop "
"Art portrait composed of enlarged half-tone dots, or even a mural on a brick "
"wall. The <menuchoice><guimenu>Image</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Apply Texture</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> Image Editor menu can be used for that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Texture Tool"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: editor-decorate.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Apply Texture Tool Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Two options give you control over the texture applying on image:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Type</guilabel>: this option specifies the decorative texture "
"style to apply under the image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Relief</guilabel>: dragging this option to the right increases the "
"appearance of depth or three-dimensionality of the texture on image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Texture tool in action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <guilabel>Paper</guilabel> texture effect apply to a photograph is "
"available below. The original image is (1), the target image is (2). "
"<guilabel>Relief</guilabel> factor used is 200."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: editor-decorate.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Texture Effect Preview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add Border"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Add Border</emphasis> is a tool to frame an image "
"with decorative borders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keeping the viewer's interest within the confines of the edges of a "
"photograph is not a simple task. One of the simplest ways to hold the "
"attention on an image is to incorporate a decorative frame around an image. "
"It acts as a kind of psychological barrier to the straying eye. The "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Image</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Add Border</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> Image Editor menu can be used for that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Add-border tool"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Four options give you control over the decorative frame rendering:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Type</guilabel>: this option specifies the decorative frame style "
"to apply around the image. <guilabel>Solid</guilabel> style just surrounds "
"the image with a colored line, <guilabel>Niepce</guilabel> style surrounds "
"the image with a fine line and a large border (ideal for black and white "
"images), <guilabel>Beveled</guilabel> style adds a neat dimension to your "
"image (ideal to create a button effect), and <guilabel>Decorative</guilabel> "
"style adds an ornamental border using patterns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Width</guilabel>: this option specifies the border width in "
"percents of image size. The border is added around the image. The width "
"range is limited between 1% and 50%."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>First</guilabel>: this option specifies the first color to use "
"with the current border type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Second</guilabel>: this option specifies the second color to use "
"with the current border type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guilabel>OK</guilabel> button to apply the border around the "
"current image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The border decorated target image will be bigger than the original, but it "
"will retain the same aspect ratio. This is important for printing images, "
"especially if you have used the Aspect Ratio Crop tool before."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Add-border tool in action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Add Border dialog tool in action is available below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: editor-decorate.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Add Border Tool Dialog in Action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Insert Text</emphasis> is a tool for adding text to "
"an image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a handy tool as it lets you add formatted text easily to an image "
"wherever you want, at several places when needed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Insert Text tool"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tool seems very intuitive to use. Type in your text and place it with "
"the mouse. Use the block settings as you please. Choose the orientation, "
"color from a color space, and fonts with all their properties. You will have "
"to scale the font size to the image size, the larger the image, the larger "
"the font has to be! Finally choose to add a border around the text and/or a "
"semitransparent background. Voilà, it's finished!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any text setting you have chosen can always be changed as long as you don't "
"click the OK button. In saved and reloaded images the text has become part "
"of the image, it cannot be changed anymore."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-decorate.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Insert Text tool in action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-decorate.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Insert Text dialog tool in action is shown below."
msgstr ""

